# Quacker Core

Quacker is a private, ad-hoc group chat for trips and conferences — short-lived social groups that need to sync quickly.

## Naming: code name vs brand

- **Quacker** is the internal **code name** — use it only for infrastructure and
  config: repo, `package.json` name, Supabase project names, env keys,
  `localStorage` keys, CI, and internal docs/rules.
- **Yowl** is the **user-facing brand** — use it in all copy an end user sees:
  UI text, page/tab titles, notifications, PWA manifest, meta tags, `alt` /
  `aria-label`, and any user-facing message. Production domain is `yowl.us`.
- Rule of thumb: if a human end user reads it, it says **Yowl**; if it's
  plumbing, it's **quacker**. Never surface "Quacker" in user-facing copy.

### Casing (do not invent variants)

| Form | Use for |
| ---- | ------- |
| **Yowl** | User-visible brand word — UI copy, titles, `alt`/`aria-label`, OG/Twitter, Playwright `getByRole` names, Maestro `visible`/`tapOn` for the brand |
| **yowl.us** | Domain / URLs only (always lowercase) |
| **yowl-…** | Asset / file kebab ids (`yowl-logo.svg`, `phone.yowl.us`) — lowercase |
| **quacker** | Repo, `package.json` `name`, env/`localStorage` key prefixes, CLI project ids |
| **Quacker** | Internal docs headings / code-name prose only — never UI |

- Do **not** use lowercase **yowl** as visible brand text (old wordmark style).
  The header logo’s accessible name is **Yowl** (image `alt`), not `yowl`.
- When branding changes, update e2e/Maestro selectors to the **accessible
  name** users/AT actually see — not a stylized spelling from an old mock.

## Stack

- Vite + `@vitejs/plugin-react-swc` (SWC, not Babel)
- React 19, Chakra UI v2, FontAwesome
- Supabase (Postgres + Realtime + Twilio Verify SMS auth)
- Path alias: `@@*` → `src/*`

## Conventions

- Pin exact semver versions in `package.json` — no carets
- Minimal diffs; match existing patterns in surrounding code
- Import Chakra via `@@ui` barrel, not `@chakra-ui/react` directly in pages
- **Agent owns all execution** — use MCP/CLI for Supabase, Vercel, GitHub; see [`.cursor/rules/mcp-first-ops.mdc`](mcp-first-ops.mdc)
- UI work follows [`.cursor/rules/ux-standards.mdc`](ux-standards.mdc) (purple-neutral / teal-action color roles, no blank states, chat layout contract)
- When adding tools or CLI workflows, update `.gitignore` for generated local paths (see [`.cursor/rules/supabase.mdc`](supabase.mdc))

## Verification

Run `yarn verify` before marking work complete.
